    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Math Camp\"\nsubtitle: \"Northwestern University -- Social Science -- Summer 2026\"\nauthors:\n  - \"[Artur Baranov](https://artur-baranov.github.io)\"\n  - \"[Gustavo Diaz](https://gustavodiaz.org/)\"\n  - \"TBD\"\nformat: \n  html:\n    page-layout: full\n---\n\n\n\n## Welcome\n\n<!-- Duke math camp syllabus  -->\n<!-- https://sites.duke.edu/daveasiegel/files/2020/07/Mathematics-for-Political-and-Social-Research-Syllabus_Siegel-1.pdf -->\n\nThis is the website for the 2025 Social Science Math Camp, hosted by the Departments of [Political Science](https://polisci.northwestern.edu/) and [Sociology](https://sociology.northwestern.edu/) at Northwestern University. The purpose of Math Camp is to give you a chance to brush up on concepts and skills that underlie the practice of quantitative data analysis in the social sciences.\n\nOur schedule features math in the morning and statistical programming in the afternoon. During lunch, we will also have a chance to meet faculty and graduate students and have more informal conversations about the role of methods training in graduate school.\n\n<!-- Here are the slides from the information session on [Research Computing and Data Services resources](rcds.pptx). -->\n\n### Details\n\n- {{< fa calendar >}} &nbsp; September 9 -- 18\n- {{< fa clock >}} &nbsp; 9:30 AM -- 4:00 PM\n- {{< fa location-dot >}} &nbsp; TBD\n\n## Schedule\n\n\n\n\n\n\n```{=html}\n<!-- preamble start -->\n\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.js\"></script>\n\n    <script>\n      // Create table-specific functions using external factory\n      const tableFns_0gx3cdjreov7es8ijb2l = TinyTable.createTableFunctions(\"tinytable_0gx3cdjreov7es8ijb2l\");\n      // tinytable span after\n      window.addEventListener('load', function () {\n          var cellsToStyle = [\n            // tinytable style arrays after\n          { positions: [ { i: '8', j: 1 }, { i: '8', j: 2 }, { i